# Messages for notifications.outbound: email, push and SMS waiting to be sent.
#
# What this topic is here for: it is the one that is read by a LIVE consumer group in the demo
# (`fraud-scoring` subscribes to it as well as to fraud.scores), so it is where you look to see a
# group's assignment spanning two topics. A group's lag is not one number, and a screen that adds
# the two topics together loses the only fact worth knowing.
#
# Its retention is six hours, the shortest on the cluster, because a notification nobody sent
# within the hour is not worth sending. That makes it the topic to open when you want to see a
# short retention window stated in the configuration tab next to a topic that keeps 180 days.
#
# The headers carry the routing decision — channel, template, priority — which is what an operator
# reads first when somebody says "the password reset emails have stopped".
#mode: headers-key-value

